# Secrets. `.env.example` is the published template; `.env` never ships.
.env
.config.rendered.*.json
# The pre-pid name is still ignored. A checkout can already hold one, with the
# keys in it, precisely because an earlier revision ignored it -- dropping the
# pattern would make that file untracked and eligible for the next `git add -A`.
.config.rendered.json

# The config loader's own bookkeeping: it writes `<config>.migrations.json`
# beside whatever config file it loaded, to record the schema version already
# applied. It is written by the runtime, read by the runtime, and carries
# nothing a checkout needs.
config.migrations.json

# Local records of an install, and of the config that preceded an update. Both
# carry this machine's absolute paths, and a backup taken through install.py
# carries every other subagent registered on it.
subagents-backup-*.json
config.json.bak-*
*.tar.gz

# The docker era. The image and its exported tarball are 1.6 GB of build
# output, and the sample deck is a rendered artifact -- none of it is source.
# Kept as patterns rather than deleted lines so a stray re-export cannot walk
# back into the repo.
*.tar
*.pptx

# The bundled templates are the exception: they are what a task with no template
# of its own is offered, so a checkout without them resolves an empty catalogue.
# They are source in the sense that matters here -- nothing in this repo builds
# them -- and they are large, so a change to this directory is a decision.
!Raven-PPT/raven/ppt/assets/templates/*.pptx

# Runtime state. Every one of these is a record of real runs -- the materials a
# caller pointed at, the decks built, the pages rendered for review -- so it is
# work data, not sample data. Anchored to this folder, because the vendored
# build below carries real packages under some of these names.
/runs/
/sessions/
/exports/
/materials/
/workspace/
/cache/
/logs/
/traces/
__pycache__/

# The vendored checkout ships, but not everything inside it.
#
# `.venv/` is the ppt extra's whole dependency set - PyMuPDF, python-pptx,
# Pillow - whose console scripts carry this machine's absolute paths baked into
# their shebangs. `uv sync --extra ppt` in the checkout rebuilds it correctly;
# a copied one fails outright.
Raven-PPT/.venv/
Raven-PPT/**/__pycache__/
